<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="theme-color" content="#101310"/><title>Privacy information — BF GYM</title><link rel="icon" href="/bf-icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"/></head>
<body><div class="wrap"><header><a href="/">BF<span>.</span> GYM</a><a href="/">← HOME</a></header><main><p class="kicker">BF GYM / PRIVACY</p><h1>YOUR DATA<br/><em>MATTERS.</em></h1><div class="notice"><strong>PRE-LAUNCH PRIVACY INFORMATION — NOT A FINALISED PRIVACY NOTICE</strong><p>BF GYM Global is preparing a worldwide online fitness website and app operated from the United Kingdom. Public coaching enquiry forms are disabled by default while business identity, contact details, lawful basis, data retention and international privacy arrangements are reviewed. We do not yet offer accounts, paid bookings or memberships.</p><p>Before enabling enquiries, the owner must publish a complete legal privacy notice with verified business contact details and data-handling practices.</p></div><h2>Private profile and membership-card preview</h2><p>Visitors can optionally enter a display name or nickname, select a general fitness interest, and add an Instagram username to create a <a href="/join/">BF profile and card preview</a>. This is <strong>not a registered online member account</strong>. The page saves this information in the visitor's browser local storage only, using the key <code>bfgym-local-profile-preview-v1</code>. It does not send the entries to BF GYM servers, publish a member directory, request passwords, or connect to Instagram. An optional Instagram handle becomes a link visible only on the same device in this preview. Visitors may erase the preview using the Erase button or by clearing site data in the browser. Avoid entering private, sensitive or health information.</p><p>The homepage links directly to existing free workout plans, exercise demonstrations and the training dashboard. It does not offer public matching, messaging or profile sharing. A valid membership card, globally accessible account, and online sign-in are not issued by the private card preview.</p><h2>Digital membership card and dashboard demonstration</h2><p>The <a href="/app/membership/">digital member card demo</a> shows an AI-generated fictional portrait and invented member information, including illustrative height, weight and BMI. The card flip and dashboard preview do not ask for or collect visitor input, do not register any client and do not issue valid membership IDs, QR tokens or Apple/Google Wallet passes. These fictional measurements are displayed publicly only as examples; no real client's health information is on the demo card. Any future real member accounts or sensitive fitness records would require new safeguards and an updated privacy notice before launch.</p><h2>What the forms request</h2><p>If the optional enquiry forms are enabled after launch, they will request your name, email, coaching preference and optional scheduling/message details. The current pre-launch website does not accept those enquiries by default. Please do not submit medical histories, diagnoses or other sensitive personal information.</p><h2>What the information is for</h2><p>If contact forms are enabled, details will be intended to allow BF GYM Global to reply to enquiries and make arrangements for requested services. They are not intended for general advertising or unrelated marketing through these forms.</p><h2>Service providers</h2><p>When deployed on Netlify, Netlify Forms may store and process enquiries. If an optional external Calendly booking link or Stripe payment link is enabled, those services process information under their own notices and policies. Customers should review those notices before using them.</p><h2>Retention and your rights</h2><p>A clear retention schedule, business identity and contact method must be added before this site is publicly launched. In the UK, individuals have data protection rights, including access to personal data and correction of inaccurate information, subject to applicable rules, and can complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office.</p><p><a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">UK Information Commissioner's Office ↗</a></p><p class="bottom"><a href="/">← Back to BF GYM</a></p></main></div></body></html>
